## 36. Git Commit Strategy

Do not make one giant commit at the end.

Use meaningful commits such as:

```text
Initial project setup
Add dataset profiling
Add data cleaning
Add database schema
Add sales calculations
Add dashboard
Add payment analytics
Add return analytics
Add upload validation
Add deployment configuration
```

---

## 37. Development Rule for AI Coding Assistants

When I ask for a feature:

1. Understand the existing project.
2. Check the existing files.
3. Reuse existing code where appropriate.
4. Do not unnecessarily rewrite working code.
5. Tell me which files will change.
6. Give the implementation.
7. Explain how to test it.
8. Wait for my confirmation before moving to another major feature.

Never overwrite working functionality without a reason.

